    "changes": [
      "Extracted device bodies and a separate Magic Keyboard accessory; excluded unrelated parts and presentation duplicates. Samsung's glTF sources (Draco decoded by Blender's glTF importer) hold one device each and keep every mesh.",
      "Normalized conventional device portrait axes, centered their screen and uniformly scaled its height to 2.2 scene units. The Duo retains its upstream centimeter hinge rig.",
      "Replaced the baked marketing screen with a named placeholder for the live framebuffer.",
      "Split the Galaxy Z Fold8 (vertical hinge) and Z Flip8 (horizontal hinge) at the hinge into two halves pivoting on the hinge axis just in front of the inner display; the inner display, its bezel and the hinge links that stand proud of the frame are cut with their halves, the spine (Hinge, SAMSUNG_LOGO) becomes a separate hinge group, and the displays become cover-display and inner-display-<side> placeholders.",
      "Resized textures to at most 1024 pixels and encoded them as WebP; retained body geometry.",
      "Re-encoded the geometry of every model except the iPhone Duo with EXT_meshopt_compression (gltf-transform meshopt --level medium: 14-bit positions, 10-bit normals); the Duo keeps float geometry because its hinge rig and display UVs depend on per-mesh local coordinates. The Samsung fold rigs are re-encoded too: their viewer reads display frames through node transforms."
    ]
  },
